NAMECHEAP PRIVATE EMAIL & DNS AUTO-RESPONSE INTEGRATION GUIDE
=============================================================
Date: 2026-11-17
Project: Valentina Alemán Portfolio (Digital Presence Assessment)
Author: GitHub Copilot × Guillermo & Valentina

1. OVERVIEW & OBJECTIVE
-----------------------
When a visitor completes the 5-question "Digital Presence Check" and submits the 
lead form ("REQUEST A PERSONALIZED REVIEW"), the system should:
  1. Receive the payload:
     - Client details: Name, Company, Email, Notes
     - 5 answers: Q1 (Website), Q2 (Visibility), Q3 (Objective), Q4 (Tasks), Q5 (Improvement)
     - Triggered recommendations: Website Design & Development, SEO, Business Automation, or Fallback
     - Timestamp
  2. Send an instant, personalized confirmation email to the user via Namecheap Private Email (SMTP).
  3. Send an internal notification email to Valentina (e.g. contact@valentinaaleman.com / valenalemanb@gmail.com) with the full client profile and diagnostic snapshot.

Since the website is hosted on GitHub Pages (static front-end), the form submission needs a lightweight, secure serverless endpoint to dispatch the emails using Namecheap's SMTP credentials.


2. NAMECHEAP PRIVATE EMAIL SMTP SPECIFICATIONS
----------------------------------------------
Domain: e.g. valentinaaleman.com (or your Namecheap registered domain)
Mailbox: e.g. hello@valentinaaleman.com / contact@valentinaaleman.com

SMTP Server Details:
- SMTP Server Host: mail.privateemail.com
- SMTP Port: 465 (SSL) or 587 (TLS/STARTTLS)
- Authentication: Required (Username = full email address, Password = mailbox password)
- Sender Address: e.g. "Valentina Alemán <contact@valentinaaleman.com>"


3. NAMECHEAP DNS CONFIGURATION (CRITICAL FOR DELIVERABILITY)
-----------------------------------------------------------
In Namecheap cPanel or Advanced DNS dashboard for your domain, ensure these records are active:

A. MX Records:
   - Priority 10: mx1.privateemail.com
   - Priority 10: mx2.privateemail.com

B. SPF Record (TXT record on @):
   - Type: TXT
   - Host: @
   - Value: v=spf1 include:spf.privateemail.com ~all

C. DKIM Record:
   - Enabled inside Namecheap Private Email settings (Generates a TXT record like default._domainkey).
   - This prevents emails sent to users from landing in their Gmail/Outlook Spam folder.

D. DMARC Record:
   - Type: TXT
   - Host: _dmarc
   - Value: v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:admin@valentinaaleman.com


4. RECOMMENDED IMPLEMENTATION ARCHITECTURES
------------------------------------------

OPTION A: Cloudflare Workers (Free, Fast, Zero Server Maintenance) - RECOMMENDED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cloudflare Workers has zero cold start, runs globally, and integrates directly with any SMTP or transactional API.

Worker Code (worker.js):
```javascript
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    if (request.method === "OPTIONS") {
      return new Response(null, {
        headers: {
          "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "https://valentinaaleman.github.io",
          "Access-Control-Allow-Methods": "POST, OPTIONS",
          "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": "Content-Type",
        },
      });
    }

    if (request.method !== "POST") {
      return new Response("Method Not Allowed", { status: 405 });
    }

    const data = await request.json();
    const { client, answers, recommendations, timestamp } = data;

    // Build the email body
    const userEmailHtml = `
      <div style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: #151515; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; line-height: 1.6;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Your Digital Presence Snapshot</h2>
        <p>Hi ${client.name},</p>
        <p>Thank you for taking the 2-Minute Digital Presence Check. Here is the initial assessment generated for <strong>${client.company}</strong>:</p>
        
        <div style="background-color: #F5F5F0; border: 1px solid #E2E2DC; border-radius: 8px; padding: 18px; margin: 20px 0;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 0;">Identified Opportunities:</h3>
          <ul>
            ${recommendations.map(r => `<li><strong>${r.title}</strong>: ${r.desc}</li>`).join('')}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p>Valentina and Guillermo will review your specific answers and reach out to discuss next steps.</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 32px; font-size: 14px; color: #666660;">
          Best regards,<br>
          <strong>Valentina Alemán</strong><br>
          Creative Strategist & Brand Director
        </p>
      </div>
    `;

    // Dispatch via SMTP or Resend/Brevo bound to Namecheap domain
    // ...
    
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {
      headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "https://valentinaaleman.github.io",
      },
    });
  }
};
```

OPTION B: Formspree / EmailJS (No backend code required)
--------------------------------------------------------
1. Register on Formspree or EmailJS.
2. In EmailJS: Connect your Namecheap Private Email account directly using SMTP host `mail.privateemail.com`, port `465`, your username and password.
3. In EmailJS Dashboard: Create an auto-reply email template with dynamic placeholders `{{name}}`, `{{company}}`, `{{recommendations}}`.
4. In `script.js`:
   Replace the placeholder `console.info` with:
   ```javascript
   emailjs.send("service_namecheap", "template_snapshot_autoreply", {
     to_name: leadName.value.trim(),
     to_email: leadEmail.value.trim(),
     company: leadCompany.value.trim(),
     notes: leadNotes.value.trim(),
     recommendations: generatedRecommendations.map(r => r.title).join(", ")
   });
   ```


5. CLIENT-SIDE SCRIPT INTEGRATION POINT
---------------------------------------
In `/home/blackbox/valentina/script.js`:
Inside `leadForm.addEventListener('submit', ...)`, around line 680:

```javascript
// Send data to endpoint
fetch('https://api.valentinaaleman.com/api/assessment-submit', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify(assessmentData)
})
.then(res => res.json())
.then(data => {
  btnSubmitLead.disabled = true;
  btnSubmitLead.textContent = '✓ REQUEST SENT';
  formFeedback.hidden = false;
  formFeedback.className = 'dp-form-feedback is-success';
  formFeedback.textContent = `Thank you, ${leadName.value.trim()} — your assessment snapshot has been emailed to ${leadEmail.value.trim()}. We will be in touch shortly.`;
})
.catch(err => {
  formFeedback.hidden = false;
  formFeedback.className = 'dp-form-feedback is-error';
  formFeedback.textContent = 'An error occurred. Please try again or email valenalemanb@gmail.com directly.';
});
```


6. CHECKLIST BEFORE ACTIVATING PRODUCTION EMAILS
------------------------------------------------
[ ] Namecheap Private Email inbox created and tested for inbound/outbound.
[ ] SPF, DKIM, and DMARC TXT records verified in Namecheap DNS.
[ ] Serverless endpoint (Cloudflare Worker or EmailJS) configured with SMTP credentials.
[ ] Auto-reply template copy reviewed and approved by Valentina.
[ ] End-to-end test submission executed and verified on Gmail, Apple Mail, and Outlook.
